    {
      "id": "sol.ahsme-1981-p4.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "The relation \\(3L=4S\\) gives \\(S=\\frac{3L}{4}.\\) Thus \\[ L-S=L-\\frac{3L}{4}=\\frac L4=8, \\] so \\(L=32.\\)\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is C.",
      "hints": [
        "Let \\(L\\) and \\(S\\) denote the larger and smaller numbers",
        "Use \\(3L=4S\\) together with \\(L-S=8\\)"
      ],
